WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.280
You probably know
the database tables

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.800
store data in the forms
of columns and rows.

3
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.195
But how do you make sure that

4
00:00:06.195 --> 00:00:08.850
every column accept the
correct type of data?

5
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.490
For instance, that
your cost column

6
00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.530
stores values in decimal while

7
00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.440
your product quantity column
accepts positive numbers.

8
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.290
This is exactly
what data types do.

9
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.835
With data types,

10
00:00:20.835 --> 00:00:22.560
you can determine
what kind of data is

11
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.840
accepted by each
field in your table.

12
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.490
Over the next few minutes,

13
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.990
you'll learn how to explain

14
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.120
the numeric data
type in a database,

15
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.720
and differentiate between
integer and decimal data types.

16
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.390
Before you begin exploring
numeric data types,

17
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.695
let's take a moment to explore
the concept of data types.

18
00:00:39.695 --> 00:00:42.005
When you create a
table in a database,

19
00:00:42.005 --> 00:00:43.970
you need to define
column names and

20
00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.440
the data type of the content

21
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.335
that will reside
in those columns.

22
00:00:47.335 --> 00:00:49.280
Data type tells the database

23
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.110
management system such as MySQL,

24
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.360
how to interpret the
value of the column.

25
00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.985
Data types maintain data
in the right format

26
00:00:55.985 --> 00:00:58.960
and make sure the value of
each column is as expected.

27
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.485
The most used data
types are numeric,

28
00:01:01.485 --> 00:01:04.285
string, and date and
time data types.

29
00:01:04.285 --> 00:01:06.050
Let's take the
example of a table

30
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.270
from the database
of an online store.

31
00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.130
This table collects information

32
00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.270
on customers in the form of

33
00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.685
columns called customer name,

34
00:01:14.685 --> 00:01:18.570
order price, product
quantity, and total price.

35
00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.930
Each of these columns
must store data in

36
00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.240
the form of a
suitable data type.

37
00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.225
The customer name column
can use string data,

38
00:01:26.225 --> 00:01:28.090
order type can use a date type,

39
00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.480
and product quantity and

40
00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.510
total price columns are best
suited to numeric data.

41
00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:35.860
The focus of this video
is a numeric data type.

42
00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.780
Numeric data types is the
generic term used for

43
00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.490
all specific data types that let

44
00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.645
a column store data as
numbers in the database.

45
00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:46.310
The two most common
numeric data types used in

46
00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.010
databases are the
integer data type,

47
00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.675
used for a whole number value,

48
00:01:50.675 --> 00:01:52.490
and the decimal data type

49
00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.600
used for number with
a fraction value.

50
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.870
To return to our
earlier table example,

51
00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.430
the product quantity column is

52
00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:00.440
defined as an integer data type.

53
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.190
This is because it holds
whole numbers only.

54
00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.300
Fractional numbers
can be inserted,

55
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.580
but they'll always be
automatically rendered up or

56
00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.225
down to the nearest whole
number of the database.

57
00:02:10.225 --> 00:02:12.835
The total price column
is a decimal type.

58
00:02:12.835 --> 00:02:15.320
This is because it holds
fractional numbers.

59
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.015
For example, an item that costs

60
00:02:17.015 --> 00:02:20.130
$80.90 is a fractional value,

61
00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:23.210
80 is a whole number
and 90 is a decimal.

62
00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.550
Whole numbers can
also be inserted.

63
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.710
The database will
add a decimal point

64
00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.915
along with a fractional
value of zero.

65
00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:32.240
In most database
management systems,

66
00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.440
you'll find different types of

67
00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.390
integer in decimal data types.

68
00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:37.370
Each type is intended to store

69
00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.380
minimum and a maximum
number value.

70
00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:42.590
For example, in MySQL
Database Management System,

71
00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:45.140
tiny integer or TINYINT

72
00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.155
is used for very small
integer number value,

73
00:02:48.155 --> 00:02:49.910
or the maximum possible value

74
00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.520
that can be inserted is 255.

75
00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.080
While integer or INT can be

76
00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.650
used to store a very big number,

77
00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.730
the maximum value that it can
store is over four billion.

78
00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.230
These data types can also

79
00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.375
accept negative and
positive values.

80
00:03:02.375 --> 00:03:04.645
In some Database
Management Systems,

81
00:03:04.645 --> 00:03:07.610
you can also force columns
to accept positive numbers.

82
00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.315
This increases the maximum
value they can store.

83
00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:11.960
You should now be
able to explain

84
00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.985
the numeric data
type in a database,

85
00:03:13.985 --> 00:03:16.550
and you should also be capable
of differentiating between

86
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:20.460
integer and decimal
data types. Great work.